feat(commands): add jujutsu integration and cmdline helpers

Extends the command system with jujutsu version control support and
enhanced command-line navigation utilities.

Adds SensibleJujutsuDescribe command that writes the current buffer to
`jj describe --stdin`, enabling commit message composition directly in
Neovim. This complements the existing SensibleGitCommitAndPush and
supports teams migrating from Git to jujutsu.

Enhances SensibleCommand by creating two new sub-commands:
- SensibleCmdlineLastCommand: Opens cmdline window on last cmd
- SensibleCmdlineBackwardSearch: Opens cmdline window in search

These improve command-line workflow by providing quick access to command
history without manual navigation through q:.

Adds .commit-stash and .prepare.yaml as workspace metadata files for
development tooling integration.

Includes commented-out SensibleShiftWidth command framework for future
tabstop/shiftwidth configuration, and adds inspirational credit
reference to willhbr's dotfiles.

